# ---- KEY MATERIAL -- GLOBAL, deliberately NOT path-scoped ------------------------------------
# This repo is PUBLIC. A private key reaching a commit is unrecoverable by deletion (it lives in
# history and must be treated as compromised + rotated), so the rule is a blanket one.
#
# WHY IT IS GLOBAL NOW (2026-07-24): the previous rule was `tools/coop-server-rs/*.pem` -- ONE level
# deep -- sitting under a comment that read "tlstest/ is ignored above". There was NO tlstest rule
# anywhere in this file; that comment was the only occurrence of the word. So
# tools/coop-server-rs/tlstest/key.pem sat untracked-but-NOT-IGNORED for four days, one `git add -A`
# away from a public commit, while the file claimed it was covered.
#
# Two lessons, both already in docs/LESSONS.md, both paid for here:
#   - a FALSE comment about a protection is worse than no comment (it stops anyone re-checking);
#   - a path-scoped key rule grows a new gap every time a subdirectory appears. Scope by ARTIFACT
#     KIND, not by location.
# If a PUBLIC cert ever genuinely needs committing, force it explicitly: `git add -f <file>`.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# user-approved site screenshots staging (user 2026-07-26): never commit
ignore_folder/

# ---- EXTRACTED GAME ART -- copyrighted, not ours to redistribute ------------------------------
# 864 KB of icons extracted from the VOTV cooked assets (kerfur skins). This repo is PUBLIC and the
# mod ships WITHOUT any original game file (principle 1), so shipping the art in the repo would be
# the same violation by a different route.
#
# WHY A RULE AND NOT A HABIT (2026-07-28): this folder was named "NEVER committed" only in prose --
# docs/OPUS_48_DISCIPLINE.md:66 and the memory index -- and appeared in NO .gitignore, i.e. it sat
# untracked-but-NOT-IGNORED, one `git add -A` from a public commit. That is exactly the shape the
# 2026-07-24 key-material block above was written about; the lesson had been recorded and not
# applied one section down. A prose rule nothing enforces is not a rule.
kerfur skins icons/

# ---- CLAIMED-ENFORCED, ACTUALLY MISSING (measured 2026-08-23) --------------------------------
# The memory index lists four never-commit rules as "ENFORCED .gitignore". Two of them were not in
# this file at all: `*.lnk` and `ref_*vps*` -- i.e. VPS reference material was sitting
# untracked-but-NOT-IGNORED, one `git add -A` from a public commit, while the index claimed cover.
# That is the THIRD time this exact shape has been paid for here (key material 2026-07-24, game art
# 2026-07-28, this). A prose rule nothing enforces is not a rule -- and an index that ASSERTS
# enforcement is worse than silence, because it stops anyone checking. Verify with
# `git check-ignore -v <path>`, never by reading a list of claims.
*.lnk
ref_*vps*
imgui.ini
# Same list, the "prose only, NOT enforced" half -- enforced now for the same reason.
docs/QUESTION_FORM_*
tools/workflows/

# ---- RESEARCH CORPUS -- private in place (USER DECISION 2026-08-21, executed 2026-08-23) -----
# "research folder also get fully offline from public repo, what else?" -- recorded in
# research/findings/tooling/votv-ue4ss-f2-migration-DESIGN-2026-08-21.md:520-524 and NOT executed
# until 2026-08-23. 420 files / 24 MB of point-in-time RE, raw session logs, crash dumps and
# screenshots. It follows the site/ pattern: files STAY on disk with their own inner git repo, so
# every reading-order pointer still resolves locally and nothing is lost -- it is simply unpublished.
#
# WHAT THE DELAY COST (measured 2026-08-23, docs/DOCS_ARC.md §1d): the origin VPS IP was sitting in
# two tracked files -- research/crash_2026-07-03_rehost_wispkill/host_..._rehost_plain.log:11085-88
# (four lines, stun/turn/signaling) and votv-connection-selector-events-pinecone-2026-06-11.md:225.
# That is the SAME class as finding A11, which purged the IP from four docs on 2026-07-24 and whose
# sweep never crossed into research/. Plus three UE4Minidump.dmp process dumps of the user's own
# machine, contents unaudited. A leak sweep scoped to one directory is a leak sweep that has not run.
research/

# ---- SECURITY REGISTER -- a working exploit map for a SHIPPING mod ---------------------------
# docs/security/ is the finding register + fix plans: 18 OPEN rows of 33 carrying exact file:line and an
# explicit "attacker -> gain" column (wipe a stranger's persistent world; evict the real host and
# receive every joiner; drive another player's desk). On a PUBLIC repo that is a ready-made map
# against a mod real people are running right now. The files STAY on disk -- CLAUDE.md reading
# order 4f still resolves locally -- they are simply not published.
#
# THREE THINGS NOT TO RE-DERIVE (measured 2026-08-23, docs/DOCS_ARC.md §1):
#   - It WAS public for ~34 days (d95683cc, 2026-07-20 .. 2026-07-30, all on origin/main). The user
#     decided NOT to rewrite history, so this is casual-discoverability removal, not secrecy. Say
#     that plainly; never describe this ignore rule as having un-published anything.
#   - Removing the map does not shrink the attack surface by one byte. The cure is closing the
#     rows (docs/DOCS_ARC.md §5), and this rule must never be cited as "security handled".
#   - Source-file comments citing TRACKER rows over a SHIPPED fix are fine and deliberately kept:
#     attribution of a CLOSED finding reveals nothing. Only OPEN-count advertising is the problem.
# If a genuinely public security document is ever wanted, it goes to the root SECURITY.md instead.
docs/security/
